# July 2025 Development Updates #2


[Reclaim Protocol](https://substack.com/@reclaimprotocol)


Jul 17, 2025


Hey devs, we're back with another fresh batch of updates across the Reclaim stack. Whether you're building mobile flows, crafting web integrations, or working with our Python SDK, there's something here that'll make your life easier.


**Here's what's hot and worth knowing:**


**JS SDK (v4.3.0)** Remember that modal that just... wouldn't leave? We fixed it. Now it actually closes when verification finishes (wild concept, right?). Plus we made mobile detection way smarter - no more desktop browsers triggering mobile flows just because you resized your window. Fewer headaches, more working code.


**Mobile SDKs (v0.10.8)** We packed in a bunch of improvements:


-


Enhanced debugging with SDK log printing


-


Webview optimizations that actually make things faster


-


Better error handling for those weird edge cases


-


Unified experience across React Native, iOS, and Android


**Python SDK (v2.0.0)** Provider versioning is here! Plus we made proof verification more reliable - no more "it worked yesterday" mysteries.


**Browser Extension (v1.0.4)** Total UI makeover time. We ditched the old look and went modern. Session IDs are now front and center with one-click copying, plus we added interactive tooltips and drag-and-drop positioning. Your debugging sessions just got way more pleasant.


