## Technical Details & Implementation


### JavaScript SDK v4.3.0 - Smart Modal Management


*Repository: [reclaim-js-sdk](https://github.com/reclaimprotocol/reclaim-js-sdk)*


**Modal Auto-Close Implementation** - Modal now automatically closes when verification completes:


```text
// Before: Modal created locally, no cleanup
private async showQRCodeModal(): Promise<void> {
const modal = new QRCodeModal(this.modalOptions);
await modal.show(requestUrl);
}


// After: Modal stored as class property and auto-closes
private modal?: QRCodeModal;


private async showQRCodeModal(): Promise<void> {
this.modal = new QRCodeModal(this.modalOptions);
await this.modal.show(requestUrl);
}


// Auto-close when proof generation succeeds
if (proofs.length === 1) {
onSuccess(proofs[0]);
} else {
onSuccess(proofs);
}
this.clearInterval();
this.modal?.close(); // ← New: Auto-close modal


```


**Improved Mobile Detection Algorithm** - Smarter device detection with better scoring:


```text
// Before: Required 3 indicators, touch detection weight 2
let mobileScore = 0;
const CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD = 3;


const isTouchDevice = 'ontouchstart' in window ||
(navigatorDefined && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0);
if (isTouchDevice) {
mobileScore += 2; // Old weight
}


// After: Requires only 2 indicators, touch detection weight 3
let mobileScore = 0;
const CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD = 2; // Reduced threshold


const isTouchDevice = 'ontouchstart' in window ||
(navigatorDefined && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0);
if (isTouchDevice) {
mobileScore += 3; // Increased weight
}


// Added new mobile-specific features detection
const hasMobileFeatures = 'ontouchstart' in document.documentElement ||
'onorientationchange' in window ||
navigator.maxTouchPoints > 1;
if (hasMobileFeatures) {
mobileScore += 2;
}


```


**Added -** Ability to close the modal manually through code.


### Mobile SDK Ecosystem v0.10.8


*SDKs Repositories: [React Native](https://github.com/reclaimprotocol/reclaim-inapp-reactnative-sdk) | [Android](https://github.com/reclaimprotocol/reclaim-inapp-android-sdk) | [iOS](https://github.com/reclaimprotocol/reclaim-inapp-ios-sdk)*


**Added Hawkeye Script:** Provider developers can now handle edge cases where certain websites block or interfere with request interception by switching interception methods via feature flags.


**Basic Request/Response Logging**


```text
// Log all requests
interceptor.addRequestMiddleware(async (requestData) => {
console.log(`📤 ${requestData.method} ${requestData.url}`, {
headers: requestData.headers,
body: requestData.body,
});
}, "request_logger");


// Log all responses
interceptor.addResponseMiddleware(async (response, requestData) => {
console.log(`📥 ${response.status} ${requestData.url}`, {
headers: response.headers,
body: response.body,
});
}, "response_logger");
```


**Request Modification**


```text
// Add authentication headers
interceptor.addRequestMiddleware(async (requestData) => {
if (requestData.url.includes("/api/")) {
requestData.headers["Authorization"] = "Bearer " + getAuthToken();
}
}, "auth_injector");


// Add CORS headers
interceptor.addRequestMiddleware(async (requestData) => {
requestData.headers["X-Requested-With"] = "XMLHttpRequest";
requestData.headers["X-Custom-Header"] = "ReclamInterceptor";
}, "cors_headers");
```


**Response Analysis**


```text
// Monitor API performance
interceptor.addResponseMiddleware(async (response, requestData) => {
const duration = Date.now() - requestData.timestamp;


if (duration > 5000) {
console.warn(
`🐌 Slow request detected: ${requestData.url} (${duration}ms)`
);
}


// Track API errors
if (response.status >= 400) {
console.error(`❌ API Error: ${response.status} ${requestData.url}`, {
response: response.body,
request: requestData,
});
}
}, "performance_monitor");
```


**Data Collection**


```text
// Collect analytics data
interceptor.addResponseMiddleware(async (response, requestData) => {
const analyticsData = {
url: requestData.url,
method: requestData.method,
status: response.status,
duration: Date.now() - requestData.timestamp,
size: response.headers["content-length"] || 0,
timestamp: requestData.timestamp,
};


// Send to analytics service
sendToAnalytics(analyticsData);
}, "analytics_collector");
```


**Request Filtering**


```text
// Block specific domains
interceptor.addRequestMiddleware(async (requestData) => {
const blockedDomains = ["malicious-site.com", "tracker.ads"];
const url = new URL(requestData.url);


if (blockedDomains.includes(url.hostname)) {
console.log(`🚫 Blocked request to: ${requestData.url}`);
// Note: Actual blocking would require additional implementation
}
}, "domain_blocker");
```


### Python SDK v2.0.0 - Provider Versioning


**Provider Versioning Support** - Added proper version management for evolving provider specifications:


```text
# Before: No version control
session_data = await init_session(
provider_id, application_id, instance._timestamp, signature
)


# After: Optional provider version support
session_data = await init_session(
provider_id, application_id, instance._timestamp, signature,
options.get("provider_version") if options.get("provider_version") else None
)


```


**Enhanced Proof Verification** - Improved handling of different witness data formats:


```text
# Before: Only handled dict format
if proof.witnesses and proof.witnesses[0].get("url") == "manual-verify":
witnesses.append(proof.witnesses[0]["id"])


# After: Handles both dict and object formats
if proof.witnesses:
first_witness = proof.witnesses[0]
# Handle both dict and WitnessData object
if isinstance(first_witness, dict):
witness_url = first_witness.get("url")
witness_id = first_witness.get("id")
else:
# Assume it's a WitnessData object
witness_url = first_witness.url
witness_id = first_witness.id


if witness_url == "manual-verify":
witnesses.append(witness_id)


```


**Simplified Parameter Handling** - Streamlined parameter validation and management:


```text
# Before: Complex parameter validation with provider config checks
def set_params(self, params: Dict[str, str]) -> None:
requested_proof = self._get_requested_proof()
current_params = self._available_params()


for param in params_to_set:
if param not in current_params:
raise InvalidParamError(f"Cannot set parameter {param}")


self._requested_proof.parameters.update(params)


# After: Direct parameter handling with simple validation
def set_params(self, params: Dict[str, str]) -> None:
validate_parameters(params)
self._parameters.update(params)


```


### Browser Extension v1.0.4 - New UI


*Repository: [reclaim-extension](https://github.com/reclaimprotocol/reclaim-extension) Look at this new UI - Now this is what clean UX looks like 🔥*


**Session ID Integration** - Session ID now passed through the entire verification flow:


```text
// Before: No session ID in popup messages
const popupMessage = {
type: 'CREATE_VERIFICATION_POPUP',
data: {
providerName,
description,
dataRequired
}
};


// After: Session ID included in popup data
const sessionId = ctx.sessionId || 'unknown';
const popupMessage = {
type: 'CREATE_VERIFICATION_POPUP',
data: {
providerName,
description,
dataRequired,
sessionId  // ← New: Session ID for tracking
}
};


```


**Modular Component Architecture** - Popup now loads HTML and CSS externally for better maintainability:


```text
// Before: HTML hardcoded in JavaScript
const popup = document.createElement('div');
popup.innerHTML = `<div class="reclaim-popup">...</div>`;


// After: External template loading
const htmlResponse = await fetch(chrome.runtime.getURL('content/components/ProviderVerificationPopup.html'));
const htmlTemplate = await htmlResponse.text();
const renderedHTML = htmlTemplate
.replace(/\\{\\{sessionId\\}\\}/g, sessionId)
.replace(/\\{\\{providerName\\}\\}/g, providerName);


```


